            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis of the Cancer-Associated KH-1 Antigen by Block Assembly of Its Backbone Structure Followed by One-Step Grafting of Three Fucose Residues.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6558-6561</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03275</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A robust, convergent, and efficient strategy was developed for the synthesis of the nonasaccharide cancer antigen KH-1. This strategy featured a one-pot block assembly of the linear hexasaccharide backbone using three disaccharides followed by grafting of three fucose residues onto the backbone in one step.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
